Message-ID: <Pine.WNT.4.64.1305171220410.1812@PC765.wehi.edu.au>

Dear Natasha,

You are trying to pass a design matrix to "classic" edgeR commands 
(estimateCommonDisp etc) that do not accept a design matrix as an argument 
and, not surprisingly, this results in an error.

If you want to specify a design matrix, regardless of the design, then you 
must use estimateGLMCommonDisp etc instead.  Please refer to the help 
pages for these functions to see what arguments can be passed.

BTW, in the current version of edgeR, there is a simpler interface 
available if you wish to use it which subsumes both the classic and GLM 
estimation routines.  You can use:

   y.filt <- estimateDisp(y.filt)

and this will work with or without a design matrix, and will compute the 
common, trended and tagwise dispersions all in one step.

Best wishes
Gordon

