Dear Richard

something to keep in mind (and I am not sure this is the issue here) is data quality (i.e. are there outliers?) and data comparability (are there drastic changes during the time?). Looking at all pairwise MA-plots (or MA-plot of each sample against an average reference (pseudo-)sample) might be enlightening. You could use the 'arrayQualityMetrics' package for that.

At best, the VST is approximate, and it may be thrown off the rails if the data's behaviour is quite different from the (negative binomial) error model.

Let us know how it goes.

        Best wishes
        Wolfgang


